    <ferc:UnappropriatedRetainedIncome id="f-757" contextRef="c-134" unitRef="u-05" decimals="0">42234030</ferc:UnappropriatedRetainedIncome>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-759" contextRef="c-02">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: 1em; text-align: inherit"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Organization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;. Effective July 1, 2024, Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;) and Sunoco LP (&amp;quot;Sunoco&amp;quot;),&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;a publicly traded subsidiary of Energy Transfer, formed a joint venture ET-S Permian Pipeline Company LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;(&amp;quot;ET-S Pipeline&amp;quot;) by combining their respective crude oil and produced water gathering assets in the Permian Basin.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt; Energy Transfer holds a 67.5% interest and Sunoco holds a 32.5% interest in the joint venture through their ownership of ET-S Permian Holdings Company LP (&amp;quot;ET-S Holdings&amp;quot;). Energy Transfer serves as the operator.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Effective July 1, 2024 the following indirect wholly owned subsidiaries of Energy Transfer merged with and into&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline: Centurion Energy Transportation, LLC, CPB Water LLC, CPB Bowser SWD #1 LLC, CPB Bowser SWD #2 LLC, RSS Water Services LLC, Panther Devco LLC, Centurion Pipeline L.P. and Centurion SENM Gathering, LP and ETP Crude LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline, Centurion Energy Transportation, LLC, Centurion Pipeline L.P. and ETP Crude LLC survived the merger.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt; CPB Water LLC, CPB Bowser SWD #1 LLC, CPB Bowser SWD #2 LLC, Centurion SENM Gathering, LP, Panther Devco LLC and RSS Water Services LLC ceased upon consummation of the merger.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Effective July 1, 2024, NuStar Permian Transportation and Storage, LLC, an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Sunoco, merged with and into&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;surviving the merger.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;operates more than 3,500 miles of crude oil and water gathering pipelines in the Permian Basin.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Regulation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline's&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;crude oil transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;) and various state authorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt; Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting policies, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Presentation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE B - SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES AND OTHER MATTERS:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt"&gt;ET-S Pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt"&gt;capitalizes expenditures related to property, plant and equipment that have a useful life greater than one year for (1) assets purchased or constructed; (2) existing assets that are replaced or improved; or (3) land regardless of cost. During construction, ET-S Permian Pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt"&gt;capitalizes direct costs, such as labor, materials, and overhead. ET-S Pipeline records property, plant and equipment at its original cost. Depreciation is computed on a composite straight-line method at the FERC authorized rates based on the expected economic lives of the various classes of assets.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligation (&amp;quot;ARO&amp;quot;)&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived assets are recorded at fair value at the time the obligations are incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. Present value techniques are used which reflect assumptions such as removal and remediation costs, inflation, and profit margins that third parties would demand to settle the amount of the future obligation. ET- S Permian did not include a market risk premium for unforeseeable circumstances in its fair value estimates because such a premium could not be reasonably estimated. Upon initial recognition of the liability, costs are capitalized as part of the long-lived asset and depreciated over the useful life of the related asset. The liability is accreted to its present value each period with accretion being recorded to operating expense with a corresponding increase in the carrying amount of the liability.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Account receivables are carried at the amount owed by customers less an allowance for credit losses. ET-S Pipeline evaluates the collectability of accounts receivable based on review of a specific customer's ability to meet its financial obligation or as a result of changes in the overall aging of accounts receivable.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline's allowance for credit losses was $0.4 million and not material as of December 31,2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Contract Balances with Customers&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. The timing of performance may differ from the timing that the associated consideration is received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract liability.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes ET-S Pipeline's fulfillment of the performance obligations. Certain contracts contain provisions requiring customers to pay a fixed fee for a right to use ET-S Pipeline's assets but allow customers to apply such fees against services to be provided at a future point in time. These amounts are reflected as deferred revenue until the customer applies the deficiency fees to services provided or becomes unable to use the fees as payment for future services due to expiration of the contractual period the fees can be applied or physical inability of the customer to utilize the fees due to capacity constraints.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Performance Obligations&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;At contract inception, ET-S Pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service that is distinct. Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline generally does not own the crude oil that it transports or stores.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline is a limited liability company that has elected to be treated as a partnership for income tax purposes. Accordingly, the tax effects of ET-S Pipeline's activities generally accrue to its members.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Environmental Expenditures&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Environmental expenditures that relate to an existing condition caused by past operations that do not contribute to current or future revenue generation are expensed. Environmental expenditures relating to current or future revenues are expensed or capitalized as appropriate. Liabilities are recorded when environmental assessments and/or clean-ups are probable, and the costs can be reasonably estimated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Remediation obligations are not discounted because the timing of future cash flow streams is not predictable. &lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE C - RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Cash Management Services&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;On September 30, 2024, ET-S Pipeline and ET-S Holdings entered into Cash Management Services agreement effective October 1, 2024 and shall continue until the close of business on October 1, 2034, unless renewed or sooner terminated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Operating Management Fees&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;ET-S Pipeline pays Energy Transfer an annual fixed operating fee as reimbursement for providing certain services including business development, legal services, accounting and financial reporting, human resource services, and other as defined in the operating agreement.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The fixed operating fee for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $30 million and $14 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE D - REGULATORY MATTERS:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;On November 26, 2024, ET-S Pipeline filed a depreciation study Docket No. DO25-5-00 to request for approval of initial depreciation rates to be effective July 1, 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;On September 4, 2025, ET-S Pipeline requested approval to revise proposed depreciation rates to be effective the first month after Commission approval. &lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 (&amp;quot;Order&amp;quot;) issued on November 20, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;In accordance with the rebillings, $13 million and $2 million have been included in operating revenues and bad debt expense, respectively, in the accompanying income statement for the year ended December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE E - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Non-cash settlement of affiliates transactions for the year ended December 31, 2025 was $818 million.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Non-cash distributions transactions for the year ended December 31, 2025 was $834 million.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures as of December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $13.7 million and $18 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Merger related non-cash contributions for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 were nil and $3 million, respectively.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
